+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_AHEAD_TWO=1 and EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_SLOTS=2: two frames in flight, each guarded (waveydude's 0927, GrowingBlackBeans' T134 merge with 0569); off by default
+
+Author of the change: waveydude (0927, branch w11-two-frame-guard, commit c8fa354). Port to T134
+and the merge with our 0569 (EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_HELD_AGE): GrowingBlackBeans
+(patches/GrowingBlackBeans/t134/0927-waveydude-ahead-guard-two-frames.patch in the public repo).
+This is his T134 file applied to T137; two hunks needed new context only (see below), no code
+changed.
+
+What it does
+EDEN_UP_AHEAD_TWO=1 (exact "1", with EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1): a present waits for the frame two
+back instead of the previous one, and never for its own (the gpu_behind second wait is off).
+EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_SLOTS=2 (exact "2", with EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=1/2/3): the copy guard gets a
+slot per frame in flight, each with its own pages, trap and fence. A copy belongs to the slots that
+needed it when it was taken; the GPU thread reads the copy of the frame the back is recording
+(BackPassed, run in order after each present's lists), failing that a newer guarded frame's copy.
+A frame's read pages end when the back passes it; what uploads read from a frame's copies goes
+back to the next gather once the back has passed it; =3 holds a write only until the back has
+passed the newest frame guarded when it was made; a present also lifts a slot whose fence is
+reached but whose fence action has not run yet. With one slot (the switch unset) the guard is
+T137's (0631 restores the last one-slot details).
+
+How it sits with 0569 (GrowingBlackBeans' merge)
+- GPU::Impl::GatherForApply: with two slots a new branch runs first: held writes carry the frame
+  they were kept for in ahead_held_frames (beside ahead_held_writes) and go out once
+  AheadGuard::StillHeld says the back has passed it; ahead_held_tags (0569's per-write tags) are
+  cleared, so ReleaseLiftedHeldLocked / EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_HELD_AGE does not run with two slots.
+  With one slot the branch is skipped and 0569's code runs unchanged.
+- AheadGuard::GuardNow (0569's view of the guard): 0927 replaced armed_frame with per-slot state,
+  so it returns the frame of the slot with the newest serial (one slot: slot 0, as before; a lifted
+  slot keeps its frame as armed_frame did).
+
+Resolved against T137 (GBB's tree has his 0918 ahead audit, ours does not)
+- nx2_gsv.h: the WaitForFrame(wait_id, wait_value) hunk had his
+  "VideoCore::GbbAheadAudit::MarkBehind" lines as context; placed by hand after the gpu_behind
+  expression.
+- ahead_guard.h ReadGpu: the comment hunk had his "GbbAheadAudit::Any()" line as context; the
+  comment change placed by hand, the code hunks applied as they are.
+
+Measured (GrowingBlackBeans, base PS5 13.60, docs/GrowingBlackBeans/read-back-race-2026-11-12.md
+and runs/GrowingBlackBeans/2026-11-12-Play2): real play, two ahead + two slots +
+EDEN_UP_AHEAD_LOAD_WAIT=1, no read sync: 29.7 fps average (one frame ahead the day before: 28.9),
+half of play at 30 fps or more (41% before), heavy windows 1% (27% before). Door-walk sessions:
+walking 24.5 -> 26.0 fps, heavy windows 77-83% -> 0. Flicker left: the read-back race (also one
+frame ahead), worst in wide shots. Without EDEN_UP_AHEAD_LOAD_WAIT=1 the first start can freeze at
+the title (3 of 6 first starts on 12 Nov); with it, none in his and waveydude's starts so far.
+
+Switches: both read once (static). Log (LOG_INFO, HW_GPU): "EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_SLOTS=2: the guard
+covers two frames in flight" once; the 300-present guard lines add "N slots, N armed beside
+another" and "N copies served both slots, N reads took a newer frame's copy" (two slots only,
+0631). Neither switch is in the shader-store stamp.
