+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] gbb: read sync census and read sync once per present (GrowingBlackBeans' 0930: EDEN_GBB_READ_SYNC_CENSUS=1, EDEN_GBB_READ_SYNC_ONCE=1, with EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC=1), off by default
+
+Author of the change: GrowingBlackBeans (0930, public repo commit c49f5ab,
+patches/GrowingBlackBeans/t134/0930-gbb-read-sync-census-and-once.patch, on his 0929 and T134).
+Applied on 0690 unchanged (gpu.cpp hunks 17 lines higher). His switch names are kept.
+
+EDEN_GBB_READ_SYNC_CENSUS=1 (exact "1", read once; needs EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC=1 and
+EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC_VERIFY=1): a measuring line. For each read read sync waits on: the time
+spent waiting for the frame's fence and in the flush round trip, the age of the last GPU write to
+the read's 64 KiB granule (0690's table, which the census fills even with 0690 off), whether the
+game read that granule in the previous present too, and whether the check found changed bytes.
+Line every 10 s: "EDEN_GBB_READ_SYNC_CENSUS: reads <n>, fence waited <n> (<ms> ms), flush <ms> ms;
+by age of the last GPU write (changed/all): <50ms a/b <100ms ... older a/b none a/b; read last
+present: changed a/b, not read last present: changed a/b". It costs what the check costs (two
+4 KiB copies per synced read) plus a table lookup.
+
+EDEN_GBB_READ_SYNC_ONCE=1 (exact "1", read once; needs EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC=1): read sync once
+per present. The first read in a present that read sync would make wait is synced as usual (fence
+wait, flush), then every range read sync read in the previous present is flushed in one more round
+trip (merged, sorted). Later reads in that present that fall wholly inside one of those ranges take
+guest memory without a wait; others are synced as usual. Each present's read ranges are the next
+present's batch. When on it is used instead of 0690 (EDEN_GBB_READ_SYNC_PENDING is not looked at).
+Line every 10 s: "EDEN_GBB_READ_SYNC_ONCE: last 10 s presents <n>, batch ranges <n>, covered <n>,
+synced <n>".
+
+Off (both unset): QueueGpuWrite tests two function-local statics instead of one; OnCPURead tests
+one more inside read sync's branch only; ReadAheadSync takes one clock reading and sets one bool
+per synced read (read sync on only). Nothing counted or logged. No shader or stamp change (names
+outside the translation sources, as 0690).
+
+Review (T153b, our reading, not measured):
+- Once trusts the first read's fence wait for the whole present: after a fence wait that timed
+  out or escaped, the later covered reads do not wait again, where full read sync would.
+- A range first read in this present still costs a full sync; the gain depends on how many reads
+  repeat from the last present (the census's "read last present" count says it).
+- The present's list of read ranges grows by one entry per read until the next present (16 bytes
+  each); bounded by reads between two presents, freed at the next one.
+- The batch flush downloads every range read last present, also those with nothing new: more
+  GPU-thread copy work in one go, but one round trip instead of about 76.
+- State of his tests: "first runs 13 Nov morning"; no results published by 13 Nov (checked against
+  his newest commit, c49f5ab, 12 Nov 22:08 UTC).
