diff --git a/tools/eglantine-patches/0700-tc-past-critical.patch b/tools/eglantine-patches/0700-tc-past-critical.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..61c34841cec3183b59dcfb9a3b21f34f263af1fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/eglantine-patches/0700-tc-past-critical.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] texture cache: the further past the critical mark, the more images a collector pass deletes (sbihaiko, Lichii #1306, EDEN_NX2_TC_PAST_CRITICAL), off by default
+
+What: past the critical mark the collector is in aggressive mode: images unused for 10 frames, 40
+a pass. Where the game makes more images than that a frame (sbihaiko: breaking pots in a later
+area makes ~55 a frame, 25 small shadow maps and the frame's targets at moving addresses, none
+replacing an older one) the cache grows ~15 images a frame, 4 GiB in two seconds, until the device
+heap is full and the driver fails the next image.
+
+With EDEN_NX2_TC_PAST_CRITICAL=1 (exact "1", read once): in aggressive mode, while the cache counts
+more than the critical mark, a pass may delete one more image for each 2 MiB past the mark (at most
+1,024 more), and from 1 GiB past the mark images unused for 3 frames go (or EDEN_NX2_TC_MIN_AGE,
+when larger). With EDEN_NX2_CLEAN_BY_TIME the extra count is multiplied by the frame-time step like
+the base count. Everything else in the pass (what may go, downloads, EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT,
+EDEN_NX2_DEFER_WRITEBACK_OOM) is as before.
+
+Note for our env: EDEN_NX2_TC_CRITICAL_MIB=3328 pins the mark (ApplyThresholdOverrides
+lets it win over the budget-following marks unless EDEN_UP_TC_BUDGET_CAP=1), and in T151 the cache
+never counted more than 2.7 GiB, so with that env this switch does not fire. It matters with a lower
+mark or with EDEN_UP_TC_BUDGET_CAP=1.
+
+Changed from his: exact "1" (his: anything but "0"); the switch is a helper (PastCriticalEnabled)
+read only in aggressive mode; placed before the CLEAN_BY_TIME step (his core has no such step).
+
+Off: one test per collector Configure, only in aggressive mode. Not in the kept-store stamp.
+
+Origin and credit: sbihaiko, EglantinePS5 branch b24-keeps, commit 91a301c ("port the patches that
+still pay on the parent's new core", his 0915 EDEN_NX2_TC_PAST_CRITICAL), after zortos293/Lichii
+PR #1306.
+---
+diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+index f1d30c5..759de42 100644
+--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
++++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+@@ -575,6 +575,12 @@ extern "C" void eden_optional_allocation_scope(bool enter) noexcept __attribute_
+     }
+ }
+ 
++// EDEN_NX2_TC_PAST_CRITICAL=1 (exact "1"): see RunGarbageCollector's Configure.
++[[nodiscard]] inline bool PastCriticalEnabled() noexcept {
++    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_NX2_TC_PAST_CRITICAL");
++    return enabled;
++}
++
+ template <class P>
+ void TextureCache<P>::RunGarbageCollector() {
+     bool high_priority_mode = false;
+@@ -600,6 +606,19 @@ void TextureCache<P>::RunGarbageCollector() {
+         ticks_to_destroy = aggressive_mode ? 10ULL : high_priority_mode ? 25ULL : 50ULL;
+         ticks_to_destroy = (std::max)(ticks_to_destroy, min_age);
+         num_iterations = aggressive_mode ? 40 : (high_priority_mode ? 20 : 10);
++        // EDEN_NX2_TC_PAST_CRITICAL=1 (sbihaiko, Lichii #1306): past the critical mark, 40 images
++        // a pass is not enough where the game makes more (in a later area ~55 a frame, at moving
++        // addresses, none replacing an older one: the cache grew ~15 images a frame, 4 GiB in two
++        // seconds, until the device heap was full). One more image for each 2 MiB past the mark
++        // (at most 1,024 more), and from 1 GiB past it images go after 3 frames unused (or
++        // EDEN_NX2_TC_MIN_AGE). Off: as before.
++        if (aggressive_mode && total_used_memory > critical_memory && PastCriticalEnabled()) {
++            const u64 over = total_used_memory - critical_memory;
++            num_iterations += static_cast<size_t>((std::min)(over / 2_MiB, u64{1024}));
++            if (over >= 1_GiB) {
++                ticks_to_destroy = (std::max)(min_age, u64{3});
++            }
++        }
+         num_iterations *= time_step;
+         // Each pass gets its own scan budget, so the aggressive pass is not starved by earlier ones.
+         num_scanned = 0;
diff --git a/tools/eglantine-patches/0701-tc-superseded-images.patch b/tools/eglantine-patches/0701-tc-superseded-images.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7cbd019cd1781d969fd02ed23b4a924c54b50711
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/eglantine-patches/0701-tc-superseded-images.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,427 @@
+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] texture cache: delete images whose memory went wholly to newer images (sbihaiko, Lichii #1314, EDEN_NX2_TC_SUPERSEDED), off by default
+
+What: the game moves its render targets within a memory pool every frame while the camera moves
+(sbihaiko counts about 45 images a frame in a later area). Each new one is a bad overlap of the
+old ones, which stay registered until the age-based collector reaches them, far slower than they
+arrive. EDEN_UP_STALE_TARGETS (0650) deletes drawn-over render targets the GPU wrote once unused
+for 10 frames; this deletes, after 2 frames unused, any image that can be proven to hold nothing a
+guest read or a join could still return.
+
+With EDEN_NX2_TC_SUPERSEDED=1 (exact "1", read once, Switch 2 titles only): every frame within 3
+frames of a new bad overlap (JoinImages) or a whole clear, TickFrame (after RetireStaleTargets,
+before AreaEvict) walks the images unused for 2 frames that have bad overlaps and classifies each
+(ClassifySuperseded, new header superseded_images.h, his, unchanged):
+- Clean: it holds no GPU data (not IsSafeGpuCopy) and its whole range lies in newer images used
+  after it: deleted.
+- Rewritten: it holds GPU data and its whole range lies in newer GPU-written images that cleared
+  their whole surface after its last write (full_write_tick, recorded by NoteWholeClears in
+  UpdateRenderTargets for a clear): deleted without a download.
+- Unproven (covered, but not by whole clears): kept, counted.
+Excluded always: sparse, unbacked, unwritten-sparse, remapped, decoding, trimmed images, images with
+aliases, CPU-modified covers. Ours: never an image something still needs, as 0650 keeps them
+(CollectStaleReferences: a queued download, an asynchronous decode or unswizzle, a bound render
+target, one of the last four presents; the present ring is now also recorded with this switch).
+The deletion is the
+collector's: untrack, unregister, DeleteImage (the memory waits for the GPU); not MarkStale (the
+covering images hold the bytes). Line every 600 frames (HW_GPU): deleted, rewritten, unproven,
+kept as still needed. Known limit (from Lichii): block-linear padding bytes that belong to no texel
+count as covered.
+
+ClearOverwritesWhole: his, with the clear-covers test of his parent core (surface clip, scissor,
+lower-left flip) written into it, since our core has no ClearCovers member; our JoinImages'
+overwritten_by_clear stays as it is.
+
+Changed from his: exact "1" (his: anything but "0"); the switch helper sits before its first use
+(his b93a1f9's fix); no PartialDownload exclusion (his 4386a82's: our core has no such flag); the
+still-needed check (0650's); the 600-frame line is in DeleteSupersededImages; deletions are traced as
+"superseded".
+
+Off: two u64 image fields that stay 0 (16 bytes per image); one static bool test per PrepareImage,
+per clear's UpdateRenderTargets, per JoinImages with bad overlaps, per present and per frame. Not in
+the kept-store stamp.
+
+Origin and credit: sbihaiko, EglantinePS5 branch b24-keeps, commits 91a301c (his 0917
+EDEN_NX2_TC_SUPERSEDED), 4386a82 and b93a1f9; after zortos293/Lichii PR #1314.
